## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical guardrail design across multi-subscription data platforms, focusing real-world constraints like admin elevation, secrets hygiene, data egress controls, governance, monitoring, and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Least-privilege RBAC with PIM
- Key Vault secrets + policy gating
- Private Link / firewall-based egress controls
- Data governance and DLP
- UEBA with Azure Sentinel
- Canary deployments and GitOps rollback

## Code Example

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Web/sites" },
        { "anyOf": [
          { "field": "siteConfig.appSettings[*].value", "like": "*SECRET*" },
          { "field": "siteConfig.connectionStrings[*].value", "like": "*SECRET*" }
        ] }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify the guardrail without affecting production?
- What telemetry and alerting would prove efficacy and catch anomalies quickly?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes automated containment and rollback for cross-region, multi-tenant Azure SaaS. Emphasizes real-time orchestration across Key Vault, AAD, RBAC, canaries, and traffic routing.

## Key Concepts

- Defender for Cloud UEBA integrations
- Event Grid and Logic Apps for automation
- Per-tenant Key Vault key rotation and token revocation
- Tenant isolation via RBAC and traffic redirection
- Canary controls and sandbox forensics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo handler for UEBA alert
async function handleUEBAAlert(event) {
  const id = event.tenantId;
  await rotateTenantKeys(id);
  await revokeTenantTokens(id);
  await setTenantRBAC(id, 'read-only');
  await pauseCanariesForTenant(id);
  await redirectTraffic(id, 'lastKnownGood');
  await cloneTenantSandbox(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this workflow end-to-end?
- How would you audit changes made during containment?
